  "domain": "infrastructure",
  "definition": "Queries, in the Logseq context, are structured Datalog or advanced query expressions embedded in pages using the `#+BEGIN_QUERY` / `#+END_QUERY` syntax. They dynamically retrieve and display blocks or pages matching specified conditions\u2014such as filtering private pages by the absence of a `#Public` tag\u2014without modifying underlying data. In the broader NarrativeGoldmine ontology, Queries represent the retrieval-layer mechanism that surfaces knowledge from the graph at read time.",
